---
description: Keep CLIENT_REFACTORING_PLAN.md status current
alwaysApply: true
---

- At the start of every task touching `Proxy Client/`, read the "Current status" block at the top of CLIENT_REFACTORING_PLAN.md and continue from "Next step".
- After each completed step, update that block: "Last updated", "Last thing I did", "Next step", and any counts you verified.
- Before stopping mid-task, update the block first.
- Edit only the status block and the relevant phase section. Never rewrite the rest of the file.
- Never mark a step done until it is verified — for the client that means verified on a live client against the unmodified server, not merely "it compiles".
- Flag a phase the moment it is blocked or contradicted, in the phase section and in the status block.
- Treat the wire protocol (packet opcodes/payloads, login handshake) and the cache format as frozen contracts: a refactor may MOVE such code but must never change what it reads or in what order. Java version is explicitly NOT part of the compatibility contract — the client and server are separate JVMs.
- Never use LWJGL `Display.setParent` to embed a GL window in the AWT frame — it is a known Windows deadlock in this codebase (see LwjglPresent).
